 "text": "Hello there! How's life treating you? It' not the best distinction, but it's practical. Glamor often involves trucking stuff around, while real wild camping isn't. That's glamping, and it' very nice. Real wild camping doesn't have that luxury. Ha, everyone starts there. A real wild camp is sleeping bag on fresh air, and that's what makes it special. If it' just a night, and you' not carried away, then yes. It's cheap and you get to see the star. I like glampers too, before someone tries turn it into resort camping. The key difference is do you bring your own food and water?",
